# Rows to merge into docs/TECH-DEBT.md

Source: Phase 2 (refactoring-patterns), first pass on `play/src/front/Phaser/Game/GameScene.ts` (2026-11-12). Baseline `HEAD` = `052f2d840`, `GameScene.ts` sha256 `6abf3d8f…4f258ef`. After the three patches: `699f7356…81650301`. Evidence: `docs/audits/tech-debt/phase2-gamescene/README.md`. Locations marked "after" are line numbers in the patched file; the others are `HEAD`'s.

## Debt Ledger: status updates

| Item | New status |
|---|---|
| GS-07 | Not dead: `onPlayerMovementEnded` is part of `ExtensionModuleOptions` (`ExtensionModule.ts:44`). `GameScene` passes it to every extension module it loads from the git-ignored `play/src/front/external-modules/` (`GameScene.ts:2711`, `play/.gitignore:35`), and those modules live outside this repository, so no search here can prove it has no caller. The API was added for them on purpose (`9988cb7a3`, "Add possibility to listen player movement for the external modules (#4890)"). The misleading comments are fixed by `02-gs07-onPlayerMovementEnded-comment.patch`: the method's comment now says that callbacks get every local move event (after `:4847-4849`). Callback behavior unchanged. Kept open as GS-09 for the name. |

## Debt Ledger: new rows

| Item | Location | Type | Risk | Effort | Priority | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| GS-09: `onPlayerMovementEnded` delivers every move event of the local player (one per frame while walking, plus each stop, turn and teleport), not the end of a movement. An extension module that trusts the name runs its callback once per frame while the user walks (inferred from `Player.moveUser`, which emits on every moving frame). Renaming it, or filtering on `moving: false`, changes the extension API that modules outside this repository use. | `ExtensionModule.ts:44`; after `GameScene.ts:4293-4295`, `:4847-4852` | design (misleading public name) | low in this repository (no in-repo caller); unknown for the external modules, which were not read | S here, plus a coordinated change in the repository that holds the extension modules | P3 | open; comment corrected in Phase 2 (`02-gs07-onPlayerMovementEnded-comment.patch`) |

